# Console live-line test — what the user types must stay the characters in front of them.
#
#   bin/metatron-console --from classes --steps bin/test/console-line-typing.steps
#
# The line the reader is editing is the user's OWN text, so graphitty markup in it is literal:
# before the <enter> AND after it.  A name in braces is not a rule, an unclosed tag does not
# swallow the line, and {{XX}} does not clear the screen out from under the cursor.  Three
# scenarios are checked, each behind its own mark so only the repaint is asserted on and never
# the original keystroke echo:
#
#   1. the echo of a submitted line — the exact shape that was reported broken:
#      """{{link}}/m/inst/+{{/link}}""" must come back verbatim, with the result on the next row
#   2. output landing mid-line, while a job is still running (the widget/trace redraw path)
#   3. a clear-screen rule typed by hand is characters, not a clear
#
# The assertion is deliberately on the literal markup: resolution SWALLOWS it, so a line that
# came back as /m/inst/+ rather than {{link}}/m/inst/+{{/link}} is exactly the failure hunted.
#
# (alt+right splitting a pane is NOT asserted on here: in split mode the line is drawn inside a
# pane whose borders clip it, so a missing string says nothing about whether it was resolved.)
#
# Colored by an ignoreGraphitty highlighter (Highlighter.line) — the same construction the
# reader's own highlighter uses for the line as it is typed.

WAIT_CONSOLE

# --- 1: the reported repro — a submitted line is echoed verbatim ---
MARK submit
SEND """{{link}}/m/inst/+{{/link}}"""
SLEEP 2
WAIT_SINCE submit {{link}}/m/inst/+{{/link}} 10
WAIT_SINCE submit '/m/inst/+' 10

# --- 2: a job's result lands while the line is being typed ---
SEND 1.sleep(second::4.0)
SLEEP 0.4
TYPE {{b}}Aldebaran{{/b}}
SLEEP 0.5
MARK typed
SLEEP 5
WAIT_SINCE typed {{b}}Aldebaran{{/b}} 10

# --- 3: a clear-screen rule typed by the user is characters, not a clear ---
# Asserted on the echo rather than on the keystrokes: jline redraws the line between keystrokes,
# so the raw characters do not arrive contiguously (the carriage returns are stripped), while the
# echo of the line is one write.
MARK clearrule
SEND {{XX}}
SLEEP 2
WAIT_SINCE clearrule {{XX}} 10
